  "snapshot": "Blender-4.2.3",
  "instruction": "Ambient Occlusion Bake\n\n`scene.blend` contains mesh `Surface` and a 512x512 image datablock `AO_Bake` already prepared as the material's bake target.\n\nBake ambient occlusion into `AO_Bake`, pack the image into the blend, and save the scene as `answer.blend`.\n\nRequirements: `AO_Bake` must remain a packed 512x512 image; the baked image must have mean gray in `[0.45, 0.90]`; the fraction of pixels below `0.3` must be in `[0.03, 0.35]`; and the image must not be flat, with gray-channel standard deviation at least `0.05`.",
  "source": "https://docs.blender.org/manual/en/4.1/; https://docs.blender.org/api/4.1/",
